      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Healthier UK</strong> is a nationwide coalition initiated by the <strong>College of Medicine</strong> and the <strong>British Society of Lifestyle Medicine</strong>. We bring together clinicians, local government leaders, charities, researchers, community champions, and policy makers who believe that a sustainable future for the UK requires a fundamental transition: from an illness-treatment model to a health-creation model.
      </p>

      <div class="highlight-box">
        <p><strong>Our Core Proposition:</strong> Health is not created in hospitals or GP surgeries &mdash; it is created in our homes, workplaces, parks, schools, and communities. When we strengthen social connections, empower local places, and invest in prevention, health becomes an asset to be grown rather than a cost to be managed.</p>
      </div>

      <img src="assets/images/feature-walking.jpeg" alt="Community members walking and talking outdoors" style="width:100%;">

      <h2>Why Health Creation?</h2>
      <p>
        For decades, health policy in the UK has focused almost exclusively on managing sickness and acute hospital demand. Despite ever-increasing budgets, public health outcomes have stagnated, health inequalities have widened, and preventable chronic illness continues to surge.
      </p>
      <p>
        Health Creation addresses the upstream determinants that keep people resilient and well:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Relational Care:</strong> Fostering strong social bonds and combating loneliness.</li>
        <li><strong>Place &amp; Environment:</strong> Expanding access to nature, green spaces, clean air, and safe active travel.</li>
        <li><strong>Community Empowerment:</strong> Investing in voluntary and community leadership rather than imposing top-down solutions.</li>
        <li><strong>Economic Resilience:</strong> Supporting good work and fair conditions that enable people to thrive.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Our vision across the four nations</h2>
      <p>
        Healthier UK works across all devolved administrations &mdash; collaborating with Mayoral Combined authorities in England, Public Health Wales and Welsh Government, NHS Scotland, and community coalitions in Northern Ireland &mdash; to share evidence, demonstrate what works, and shift funding towards prevention.
      </p>

